N('old-state-house-providence','Old State House','Providence','riprov','civic','standing',41.82889,-71.40944,'site','view','drive','','1762',
  'A brick Georgian building largely completed in 1762 and used by the colonial and state legislatures for 149 years. Meeting here on May 4, 1776, the General Assembly renounced its allegiance to the Crown. It is on College Hill, with its front to North Main Street.',
  'Brick; the colour was not checked. The former Council Chamber is the only room that keeps its original furnishings.',
  '',
  'At 150 Benefit Street. Whether and when visitors may go in was not checked here. Parking was not checked.',
  [W('Old State House (Providence, Rhode Island)')], brick='?'),
N('capitol-williamsburg','Capitol (reconstruction), Colonial Williamsburg','Williamsburg','va','civic','standing',37.27166,-76.69329,'exact','view','drive','','1934',
  'A reconstruction, built in the early 1930s, of the first of two capitols that stood on this site: the first from 1705 until it burned in 1747, the second from 1753 to 1780, when Virginia moved its capital to Richmond. Wikipedia notes that the copy has now stood longer than both originals together.',
  'A 1930s rebuilding of the 1705 capitol, part of the restoration of Colonial Williamsburg. Interior not checked.',
  '',
  'Part of Colonial Williamsburg. How visitors get in was not checked here. Parking was not checked.',
  [W('Capitol (Williamsburg, Virginia)')], brick='?'),
N('old-capitol-building-olympia','Old Capitol Building','Olympia','wa','civic','standing',47.04292,-122.89956,'exact','view','drive','','1892',
  'Built in 1892 to the design of Willis Ritchie, in the Richardsonian Romanesque style, and first known as the State Capitol Building. On the National Register since 1975. The Office of the Superintendent of Public Instruction works in it.',
  'Interior not checked.',
  '',
  'A state office building at 600 Washington Street SE. Whether and when visitors may go in was not checked here. Parking was not checked.',
  [W('Old Capitol Building (Olympia, Washington)')], brick='?'),
N('iolani-palace','ʻIolani Palace','Honolulu','hi','civic','standing',21.30667,-157.85889,'exact','open','drive','','1879–1882',
  'The palace of the rulers of the Kingdom of Hawaiʻi: the cornerstone of the present building was laid on December 31, 1879 and it was finished in November 1882. After the monarchy was overthrown in 1893 it served as the capitol of the Provisional Government, the Republic, the Territory and the State of Hawaii. Restored, it opened as a museum in 1978. A National Historic Landmark.',
  'Brick with a concrete facing. Interior not checked.',
  '',
  'Restored and open to the public as a museum since 1978 (Wikipedia). Opening hours were not looked up: see its own page before you go. Parking was not checked.',
  [W('ʻIolani Palace')], brick='no', hours='?'),
